---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { DIGUP_UI, SITE } from '../../lib/site';
---
<Layout
  title={'Install DigUp on Mac — brew install / Homebrew & DMG'}
  description={'Install DigUp on Apple Silicon (macOS 14+): brew install --cask arahim3/tap/digup, or DigUp-0.6.1.dmg. First-run model (~865 MB) and ⇧⌘Space.'}
  canonicalPath="/install-mac/"
  lang="en"
  ogImage={DIGUP_UI.hero.src}
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="meta-line"><span class="badge">Mac · {SITE.downloads.macVersion}</span> · Install guide</p>
      <h1>Install DigUp on Mac with Homebrew or DMG</h1>
      <p class="lead">Apple Silicon Macs on macOS 14 or later. Prefer <strong>Homebrew</strong> (<code>brew install --cask arahim3/tap/digup</code>), or download the DigUp DMG.</p>
    </header>

    <article class="wide">
      <div class="cta-bar">
        <a class="cta" href={SITE.downloads.mac} rel="noopener noreferrer" download>Download DigUp for Mac</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/install-windows/">Windows (beta)</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/install-linux/">Linux (beta)</a>
      </div>

      <figure class="shot-panel" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        <span class="shot-label">After install · Mac search panel</span>
        <img src={DIGUP_UI.hero.src} width="1200" height="800" alt={DIGUP_UI.hero.altEn} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption class="shot-caption">Hotkey ⇧⌘Space opens this panel.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Detail</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Chip</strong></td><td>Apple Silicon (M-series). Intel Macs are not supported by the DigUp Mac build.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>OS</strong></td><td>macOS 14 (Sonoma) or later</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Disk / network</strong></td><td>~865 MB for the EmbeddingGemma 2 model on first run; stable download path. See <a href="/embeddinggemma-2/">EmbeddingGemma 2</a> and the <a href="/guides/embeddinggemma-2-local-multimodal-search/">multimodal guide</a>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Version</strong></td><td><strong>{SITE.downloads.macVersion}</strong> stable · asset <code>DigUp-0.6.1.dmg</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 id="homebrew">Install DigUp with Homebrew (recommended)</h2>
      <p class="muted">Official tap from ARahim3 (issue <a href="https://github.com/ARahim3/DigUp/issues/2" rel="noopener noreferrer">#2</a>). Core <code>homebrew/cask</code> listing is expected after DigUp’s repo is ~30 days old (~Nov 7, 2026). The tap works now.</p>
      <pre><code>{SITE.brewCommand}</code></pre>
      <ol class="checklist">
        <li>Run the command above in Terminal.</li>
        <li>Launch DigUp from Applications / Spotlight; complete first-run model download (~865 MB) and folder picks.</li>
        <li>Hotkey: <strong>⇧⌘Space</strong>.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Alternate: DMG download</h2>
      <ol class="checklist">
        <li>Download <a href={SITE.downloads.mac} rel="noopener noreferrer" download><code>DigUp-0.6.1.dmg</code></a> (direct Release asset).</li>
        <li>Open the DMG and drag DigUp to Applications.</li>
        <li>Launch DigUp; complete first-run model download and folder selection.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>First-run checklist</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>Model download (~865 MB)</strong> — required once; stays on device.</li>
        <li><strong>Pick folders</strong> — only selected folders are indexed; undownloaded cloud placeholders are skipped.</li>
        <li><strong>Time estimate</strong> — DigUp estimates the first pass from a quick speed check on your Mac.</li>
        <li><strong>Hotkey</strong> — search panel: <strong>⇧⌘Space</strong> (Shift + Command + Space).</li>
        <li><strong>Keyword boost</strong> — exact strings (invoice IDs, error codes) still help; try natural language for photos and PDFs.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>Network blocks the model download</strong> — In Settings → Storage, use <strong>Use Files…</strong> to point at the two model files you downloaded elsewhere (added in 0.6.1). DigUp verifies them before use.</li>
        <li><strong>IME / composed text</strong> — 0.6.1 fixed Korean/Japanese/Chinese composition breaking the search field.</li>
        <li><strong>Folder names with accents / CJK</strong> — 0.6.1 fixed indexing stopping for all folders when one path had non-ASCII names.</li>
        <li><strong>Updates</strong> — DigUp → Check for Updates…, or reinstall from the latest Release asset.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Plain-English release summary: <a href="/changelog-notes/">Changelog notes</a>. See <a href="/changelog-notes/">changelog notes</a> for a summary.</p>

      <h2>Sourced numbers (2026-10-15)</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Fact</th><th>Value</th><th>Source</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Mac version</td><td>0.6.1</td><td>ARahim3/DigUp Releases</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Model download</td><td>~865 MB</td><td>Upstream README / release notes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Stars</td><td>~3,716</td><td>GitHub API</td></tr>
          <tr><td>License</td><td>MIT</td><td>Repo</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="cta-bar">
        <a class="cta" href={SITE.downloads.mac} rel="noopener noreferrer" download>Download DigUp for Mac</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/faq/">FAQ</a>
      </div>

      <section class="related">
        <h2>Also install</h2>
        <div class="cards">
          <a class="card" href="/install-windows/"><h3>Windows (beta)</h3><p>0.7.0-beta.1 setup</p></a>
          <a class="card" href="/install-linux/"><h3>Linux (beta)</h3><p>.deb and AppImage</p></a>
          <a class="card" href="/vs-spotlight/"><h3>vs Spotlight</h3><p>When to use both</p></a>
          <a class="card" href="/embeddinggemma-2/"><h3>EmbeddingGemma 2</h3><p>Model download &amp; runtime</p></a>
          <a class="card" href="/guides/use-cases/"><h3>Use cases</h3><p>By role playbooks</p></a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
